Dockerfile for Apache on App Server 1
Problem: Create a docker file /opt/docker/Dockerfile on App server 1 to build an image with ubuntu:24.04 base, install apache2 and configure it to work on 8089 port.

Solution:

bash
# Create directory
sudo mkdir -p /opt/docker
cd /opt/docker

# Create Dockerfile
sudo nano /opt/docker/Dockerfile
Dockerfile content:

dockerfile
FROM ubuntu:24.04

# Install apache2
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y apache2 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Change Apache port from 80 to 8089
RUN sed -i 's/Listen 80/Listen 8089/' /etc/apache2/ports.conf

# Update vhost to match new port
RUN sed -i 's/<VirtualHost \*:80>/<VirtualHost *:8089>/' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf

EXPOSE 8089

# Run Apache in foreground
CMD ["apache2ctl", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]
bash
# Build the image
sudo docker build -t nautilus-apache-8089 .

# Test run
sudo docker run -d -p 8089:8089 --name nautilus-test nautilus-apache-8089
curl http://localhost:8089
